# DTF tier manifest: upgrade (upgrade-with-legacy-data, matrix row 6)
# Profile-set: s3 / single. The #2574/#2584 regression class (legacy ROW-LESS
# Maven objects breaking / leaking across a cloud-storage upgrade) only manifests
# on a real shared object store, so this tier reuses the isolation tier's
# storage.s3 profile and its cross-tenant assertions.
#
# UNLIKE every other tier, `upgrade` drives a TWO-PHASE compose itself (see
# oracle.sh): it stands the stack up on an OLD pre-attribution backend, seeds the
# row-less legacy Maven shape, then swaps ONLY the backend container to the
# candidate image (--backend-image, exported as BACKEND_IMAGE) against the SAME
# postgres+minio volumes and lets migrations run. run.sh still health-gates an
# initial `up` on the candidate; the oracle tears that down (`down -v`) and
# rebuilds from the OLD image, which is a legitimate tier-specific pattern
# explicitly scoped to this tier (run.sh is NOT modified).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the seed + oracle drive many admin/alice logins and
# Maven PUTs back-to-back through a single admin; the base default (ON) would
# throttle them. Matches the isolation tier / proof rig. (Base default stays ON;
# a tier disabling a shipped control does so explicitly, per design 2.2.)
#
# UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE: the pre-#2574 "legacy deployment" backend the stack is first
# stood up on. It must be a clean migration ANCESTOR of the candidate (its applied
# migrations are an exact-checksum prefix of the candidate's set) so the in-place
# volume upgrade runs the candidate's NEW migrations instead of erroring on a
# divergent history. nexus2457-v157base (release/1.5.x line, migrations 151-154,
# NO maven_flat_object_owner attribution table) is that ancestor for the fixed
# candidate v158-4fix (adds attribution migration 155). See MATRIX-ROW.md for the
# image-lineage rationale and why base-2504 (the isolation coder's pre-#2504
# image) canNOT be used as the OLD image here.
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE="${UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE:-ak-backend:nexus2457-v157base}"
